{"ref":"BDB, מִקְרָא²","hw":"מִקְרָא²","html":"<big><span dir=\"rtl\">מִקְרָא</span></big><sub>23</sub>  <strong>n.m.</strong> <a data-ref=\"Exodus 12:16\" href=\"/Exodus.12.16\">Ex 12:16</a> <strong>convocation, convoking, reading</strong>;—<span dir=\"rtl\">מ׳</span> abs. <a data-ref=\"Isaiah 1:13\" href=\"/Isaiah.1.13\">Is 1:13</a>; <a data-ref=\"Nehemiah 8:8\" href=\"/Nehemiah.8.8\">Ne 8:8</a>; cstr. <a data-ref=\"Exodus 12:16\" href=\"/Exodus.12.16\">Ex 12:16</a> +; pl. cstr. <span dir=\"rtl\">מִקְרָאֵי</span> <a data-ref=\"Leviticus 23:2\" href=\"/Leviticus.23.2\">Lv 23:2</a> +; sf. <span dir=\"rtl\">מִקְרָאֶהָ</span> (Ges<sup>§ 91 k</sup>) <a data-ref=\"Isaiah 4:5\" href=\"/Isaiah.4.5\">Is 4:5</a>;—<br><strong>1.</strong>  <em>convocation, sacred assembly</em> <a data-ref=\"Isaiah 1:13\" href=\"/Isaiah.1.13\">Is 1:13</a> (after <span dir=\"rtl\">קְרֹא</span>), <a data-ref=\"Isaiah 4:5\" href=\"/Isaiah.4.5\">4:5</a>; usually explicitly <span dir=\"rtl\">מ׳ קֹדֶשׁ</span>, term. techn. in P for religious gathering on Sabbath and certain sacred days, <a data-ref=\"Exodus 12:16\" href=\"/Exodus.12.16\">Ex 12:16</a><sup>(×2)</sup> + 14 times <a data-ref=\"Leviticus 23\" href=\"/Leviticus.23\">Lv 23</a>; <a data-ref=\"Numbers 28\" href=\"/Numbers.28\">Nu 28</a>, <a data-ref=\"Numbers 29\" href=\"/Numbers.29\">29</a>, + (pl.) <a data-ref=\"Leviticus 23:2\" href=\"/Leviticus.23.2\">Lv 23:2</a>, <a data-ref=\"Leviticus 23:4\" href=\"/Leviticus.23.4\">4</a>, <a data-ref=\"Leviticus 23:37\" href=\"/Leviticus.23.37\">37</a>.<br><strong>2.</strong>  (n. verbi, as Aramaic Inf., Ges<sup>§ 45 e, cf. 115d</sup>) <em>convoking</em>, <span dir=\"rtl\">מ׳ הָעֵדָה</span> <a data-ref=\"Numbers 10:2\" href=\"/Numbers.10.2\">Nu 10:2</a>.<br><strong>3.</strong>  <em>reading</em> <a data-ref=\"Nehemiah 8:8\" href=\"/Nehemiah.8.8\">Ne 8:8</a>.","next":"BDB, קָרָא²","prev":"BDB, קְרִיאָה"}